# 8. What Happens During One Request?

Suppose:

```text
frontend → backend:8080
```

## Step 1 — DNS Resolution

Frontend asks:

```text
backend
```

CoreDNS responds with the Service IP:

```text
10.10.20.100
```

Therefore:

```text
CoreDNS
   |
   +---- backend → 10.10.20.100
```

---

## Step 2 — Service

Frontend sends traffic to:

```text
10.10.20.100:8080
```

This is the Kubernetes Service.

---

## Step 3 — kube-proxy

`kube-proxy` uses its node networking rules to select a backend Pod.

```text
                 10.10.20.100
                     |
             kube-proxy rules
                     |
              +------+------+
              |             |
          Pod 10.10.2.20  Pod 10.10.3.25
```

---

## Step 4 — CNI

The underlying CNI networking provides connectivity from the source Pod/node to the destination Pod.

```text
Frontend Pod
     |
     | CNI networking
     v
Backend Pod
```

---

## Step 5 — NetworkPolicy

If network policies are configured, Calico/network-policy enforcement determines whether the traffic is allowed.

```text
ALLOW → Continue
DENY  → DROP
```

---

## Step 6 — Istio

If Istio is enabled, the request passes through the Envoy proxies according to the Istio traffic architecture.

Istio can then apply:

```text
mTLS
Retry
Timeout
Traffic splitting
Authorization
Telemetry
```

---

# 9. Interview Cheat Sheet

Remember this:

```text
CoreDNS     → "Where is backend?"
kube-proxy  → "Which backend Pod?"
CNI         → "How do I reach that Pod?"
Calico      → "Is this network traffic allowed?"
Istio       → "How should this service communicate?"
```

### One-line interview answer

> **CoreDNS resolves the Service name, kube-proxy handles Service-to-Pod forwarding, the CNI provides the underlying Pod networking, Calico can enforce network-level policies, and Istio manages application-level service-to-service traffic.**

## Key Difference

| Component      | Main responsibility                                                 | Layer               |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- |
| **CoreDNS**    | DNS resolution                                                      | DNS                 |
| **kube-proxy** | Service → Pod forwarding                                            | Service/network     |
| **Azure CNI**  | Pod networking                                                      | Network             |
| **Calico**     | Network policy/security and, depending on configuration, networking | Network             |
| **Istio**      | Service-to-service traffic management                               | Application/service |
| **Envoy**      | Data-plane proxy used by Istio                                      | Application/service |

### Easy mental model

```text
CoreDNS
   ↓
"Find the service"

kube-proxy
   ↓
"Find/select the backend Pod"

Azure CNI
   ↓
"Provide Pod network connectivity"

Calico
   ↓
"Enforce network-level rules"

Istio
   ↓
"Control how services communicate"
```







